REL-AUTH-01 :: {"criterion": "`release plan --from-release-commit <sha> --decision <path>` takes the package and version roster from the decision file committed in that commit. It does not re-run changeset, group, cascade or pre-release selection."}

REL-AUTH-02 :: {"criterion": "`release plan --from-release-commit` fails with E165 and writes no output file in any of these cases: HEAD is not the given commit; the commit neither adds nor modifies the decision file; it deletes no direct-child changeset `.md` file (nested Markdown files and `README.md` do not count); a claimed package's manifest does not change to its claimed version; a claimed package's changelog is unchanged; an unclaimed manifest version changes; a claimed package is not found; or the commit changes any path other than a manifest (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, `pyproject.toml`) or lockfile (`Cargo.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`, `bun.lockb`, `uv.lock`, `poetry.lock`, `pdm.lock`) anywhere, a package's changelog, the decision file, a direct-child changeset, or the changesets directory's `pre.json`.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-03 :: {"criterion": "A committed decision file whose digest does not match its entries fails with E166. Each target version is parsed using the grammar of its package ecosystem; durable operation IDs, artifact slots and registry observations bound to an operation use that same grammar. Version values remain strings on the wire, and decision schema versions 1 and 2 are accepted; any other version fails with an error naming the version found.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-04 :: {"criterion": "An abbreviated or unknown `--from-release-commit` SHA, a non-40-hex `--orchestration-revision` for a source with `[release]`, or an `--intent` file with a different `schemaVersion` (`E215`, naming found and expected versions) fails before any output file is written or any effect runs.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-05 :: {"criterion": "`release plan` and `release execute` require the source checkout at a detached HEAD and fail with E170 otherwise. `callisto release` accepts an attached HEAD. Every route requires a complete, non-shallow SHA-1 repository and fails with E265 for a repository that is not SHA-1 and E266 for a shallow one.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-06 :: {"criterion": "`release execute` re-derives the plan from the source checkout and fails with E124 before any effect when the result differs from the `--intent` file. A change to the decision, source commit, manifests, config, registry binding or origin remote is enough.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-07 :: {"criterion": "Before each operation, the executor re-checks HEAD, worktree cleanliness and the `origin` push URL. A change stops the run before that operation's effect, with E124 for a moved HEAD or a changed `origin` push URL, E132 when `origin` has lost its push URL, and E267 for a dirty worktree.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-08 :: {"criterion": "`release plan` for a source with `[release]` requires `--orchestration-revision` and `--artifact-repository` (`E231`). For a source without `[release]` it ignores both flags, prints a notice, and plans zero artifact slots.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-AUTH-09 :: {"criterion": "`[release].forge-repository` is the only GitHub destination. Planning rejects an `--artifact-repository` that differs from it (`E230`) or from the `origin` GitHub repository (E175). Execution rejects artifact slots that target another repository, and a `[release]` section without it fails planning with E198.", "is_error_case": true}

REL-PR-01 :: {"criterion": "`release-pr decide` returns `noop` when there are no pending changesets. It returns `update` when one open PR from the same repository has head `<release-branch>` or `<release-branch>--<40 lowercase hex>`, and `create` otherwise."}

REL-PR-02 :: {"criterion": "`release-pr decide` fails in these cases: pre mode (E318, because a release PR cannot consume the changesets pre mode keeps), an invalid `--repository` flag (E141), an unsafe branch name (E142), duplicate PR numbers (E143), a snapshot for another repository or base branch (E144), a managed-branch PR from a fork (E145), more than one managed PR (E146), a malformed SHA suffix (E147), or a PR headed at `<release-branch>--staging` (E154). Each of these carries its own code even when `--snapshot`/`--decision` is a file, inline JSON, or stdin, except that an invalid repository inside that JSON fails with E281 as malformed JSON. `release-pr verify` accepts either the bare decision wire or unchanged `release-pr decide --format json` output through all three input forms. Report metadata, when present, contains both `command: release-pr decide` and boolean `dryRun`; unknown or dupli

REL-PR-03 :: {"criterion": "`release-pr commit-plan` resolves the repository root with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, so it works from any subdirectory of the checkout, and emits base64 additions and deletions for the index staged against `--base-commit`. Each added or modified regular file's bytes are hashed without filters and verified against the index blob sha before they are emitted; a worktree file edited again after staging, or whose staged blob differs because a filter changed its bytes, fails the read (E059) rather than emitting content that does not match what is staged. It fails for: no changes (E149); a mode other than 100644, where a symlink or submodule fails before any content is read (E150); a type change or unmerged path (E151); over 4 MiB of content (E152); or a path under `.github/workflows/` or `.git/`, an absolute path, or one containing `..` (E153).", "is_error_case": true}

REL-PR-04 :: {"criterion": "The release-PR action runs the version command with `--emit-decision <decision_path>` (default `.callisto/release-decision.json`). It commits the result with GitHub's `createCommitOnBranch` on `<release-branch>--staging` reset to the base commit, and refuses unless the remote tree equals the locally staged tree. It then moves the release branch ref through the REST API and never runs `git push`. Before creating the commit, before moving the ref, and before any label or PR write, it runs `callisto release-pr verify` against a fresh snapshot and stops when verification fails. After an update ref move is read back successfully, the final check supplies `--applied-head <new_sha>`. This accepts only a consistent update decision's selected PR changing to that exact head; any other snapshot change, wrong applied head, or create/noop use fails E148. The final check is retried up t

REL-PR-05 :: {"criterion": "`callisto-action` with `mode: release` runs `callisto --format json release --receipt <tmp>` and sets `published` and `publishedPackages` from registry and platform publish operations whose outcome is `published`. A `mode` other than `version-pr` or `release` fails the step."}

REL-PR-06 :: {"criterion": "With `source: auto`, `callisto-action` and `setup-callisto` default `version` input `latest` installs the callisto release the action's own invocation is pinned to (`github.action_ref` resolved against `orin-dx/callisto`'s `callisto@` tags), falling back to the newest published release only when that ref is unset or matches no tag. A failed tag lookup fails the step. An explicit `version` input overrides this resolution, including inside a Callisto checkout. A consumer manifest mentioning callisto-cli never selects a local build. `source: local` ignores version pins and requires Git-tracked Callisto source at the checkout root plus Cargo metadata confirming the local callisto-cli workspace member, manifest path and callisto binary target. Local builds use explicit manifest and output-directory paths; invalid local source fails without falling back to a downloaded or regist

REL-PR-07 :: {"criterion": "`--format json` output of `release-pr verify`, `release-pr decide` and `release-pr commit-plan` (without `--out`) goes through the same envelope every other command's JSON report uses: a top-level `schemaVersion`, `command` and `dryRun`, alongside that subcommand's own payload fields unchanged. `release-pr verify --decision` accepts `release-pr decide --format json` output as-is."}

REL-PR-08 :: {"criterion": "The release-PR action retries a forge call that fails with a transient GitHub error (`Something went wrong`, an HTTP 5xx, a gateway or timeout error, a reset or truncated connection) up to 4 attempts, waiting 2, 4 and 8 seconds, and prints a failed attempt's stderr, except for the two probes whose failure is an expected branch (resetting the staging branch and creating a ref that may already exist). A failure of any other kind is not retried. Every call is retried except `gh pr create`, and cleanup of the staging branch. Before each retry of the `createCommitOnBranch` mutation, the staging branch is put back on the base commit. A failed read of the open pull requests, including the one before each verification, stops the action with the failing `gh` call's own error and status."}

REL-PR-09 :: {"criterion": "On every push to `main`, the hold workflow converts each open, non-draft release PR (head `<release-branch>` or `<release-branch>--<anything>` in this repository) to a draft. The release-PR action creates a new PR as a draft and marks a PR ready only after the update or creation succeeded and the base branch still points at the commit the PR was built from; if the branch moved during the run, a ready PR is converted back to a draft and the action warns. A release PR whose refresh failed or never ran therefore stays a draft, and a draft cannot be merged."}

